  "_commission_comment": "0.95/side ($1.90 round turn), corrected 2026-08-24. Was 0.59, which under-charged every day's net by $0.72 per contract and left the app's balance drifting ABOVE the broker's. Two independent confirmations of 0.95: (1) replaying Tradovate's own Performance export for 2026-08-17..21 (97 round trips, 193 contracts) at 0.95/side yields a 5-day total of 811.80, i.e. a base balance of $50,811.80, which equals the broker's own start-of-day net liq to the cent (51,211.50 minus its Total P/L 399.70); at 0.59 it yields 950.76, off by exactly 193 x $0.72 = $138.96. (2) the same replay puts 2026-08-20 at -264.10, which is exactly the figure on Tradeify's own P&L calendar already recorded in tv-broker-feed.js's header from a separate source. Do NOT change this back without new evidence of the same standard: it feeds csvApply, day-rollup and the live P&L cross-check.",
