    "_comment": "ADDED 2026-08-15. The eval/funded risk layer, applied AFTER scalperRules — see stage-rules.js for the full derivation and the fail-safe argument. Anoop's strategy, verbatim: 'I want to risk aggressively in evaluation and be very secure when I'm creating a funded account, safe in funded... Spend less time in evaluation, more time in funded.' eval PERMITS upward from the base; funded CLAMPS and can only ever tighten (same one-way-ratchet idea as lossRatchet.mode 'min'). Trade COUNT is intentionally absent from the eval block so that being in eval can never raise the count above what the trading mode allows.",
