  "_autonomyEnabled_comment": "SET FALSE 2026-08-26 at Anoop's instruction (\"disable shadow mode and control mode until i start working on them and have a proper plan... i want only you mode from now on\"). RE-ENABLED 2026-09-01 at his instruction to forward-test Playbook C (ADX) - which is the proper plan that condition asked for, and it is the FIRST strategy here with out-of-sample evidence. What re-enabling does NOT change: shadowOnly still holds, liveSize is still null, and assist/control remain enabled:false, so the ONLY thing switched on is recording. Nothing here can place an order. The two objections that closed it in August are both answered: NOISE - autonomyModes.shadow.silent stays true, so no tickets reach the chat and the badge does not change mid-session, which was the actual complaint (\"it has created confusion when i was trading live\"); CHART CONTENTION - the new C-ADX monitor is cache-read only and issues ZERO CDP calls, and the shadow resolver still yields (15-min, never during a session window, never while the chart lock is held). Anoop keeps a live UI toggle: OFF and SHADOW both render, so he can drop to \"you are trading\" for his New York session and back afterwards without a restart - cadxCheckOnce() returns 'inactive' on the next tick, so OFF genuinely stops the work rather than hiding it. Set false to kill the whole thing again; DATA/autonomy/ keeps its record either way.",
