  "_autonomyModes_comment": "ADDED 2026-08-29 (AUTONOMY_MODES_SPEC.md). 2026-09-01: shadow.enabled flipped TRUE to forward-test Playbook C (ADX); assist and control stay false and therefore stay unrendered. Shadow is GLOBAL - it hooks armSetup, so A, B and LTF-ENGULF record alongside C-ADX. That is deliberate (Anoop, 2026-09-01: \"i do not have issue if same live feed is fed to both the modes\"): a record of the new rule with no record of the rules he already trades gives nothing to compare it against, and silent:true means the extra rows cost him no attention.  Per-mode flags UNDER the autonomyEnabled master switch, so the four modes can be finished and turned on one at a time. A mode with enabled:false is NOT RENDERED AT ALL - not a greyed-out button; a visible switch that does nothing invites a click that silently fails. sizes:[2] everywhere replaces the old dshV2.shadowSizes [4,6], which was the reason shadow had produced ZERO scored orders in its entire life: at $300 perTradeMaxLoss and $2/point, 4c allows only a 37.5-point stop and 6c only 25, while real Playbook B stops measure a 48.3-point median (range 38.8-72.8, see app/scripts/risk-dist.js), so EVERY setup was stamped blocked:risk-too-big and excluded from the resolver. 2 is Anoop's real sizeCap and sizeFloor, so the record needs no translation to be believed. shadow.silent was TRUE from 2026-08-29 and is now FALSE (2026-09-01, Anoop: \"All the data when goes to shadow should be from live feed so that actions and signals are give to me immediately\"). This REVERSES the August silence decision knowingly: silence was the fix for tickets confusing him mid-session on 2026-08-26, and un-silencing brings that risk back. What makes the trade acceptable is that he now has a live OFF switch he did not have then - OFF and SHADOW both render, so he drops to \"you are trading\" for his New York session and re-arms after, per-session, no restart. Silence hid the signals for ~8 weeks; a toggle he controls gets him the signals AND a way to stop them, which is what he actually asked for. If tickets start confusing live sessions again the fix is to use the toggle, or set this back to true - not to remove the feature. CONTROL's perTradeRiskCapUsd is 200, deliberately TIGHTER than the global perTradeMaxLoss of 300: its dailyLossCeilingUsd is also 200, and a daily limit is only a CEILING if per-trade risk divides into it - at the general $300 cap a single stop-out could lose $291 and overshoot the stated ceiling by 46% before anything could halt it. At $200/trade and $200/day CONTROL gets exactly ONE full loser per day and the ceiling is real (overshoot is slippage only). Cost: it skips the widest ~33% of Playbook B setups. autoResetDaily:false is Anoop's decision of 2026-08-29 - once tripped, CONTROL stays demoted to SHADOW until he personally re-arms it, because a breaker that resets on a timer lets a bad week run five unattended days. NOTE evidence read FOR CONTROL must filter shadow rows to riskUsd <= 200, since SHADOW records under the looser $300 cap. 2026-09-01: control.playbooks trimmed from [A,B,LTF-ENGULF] to [A,B]. Not a reduction in scope - every always-on engulf watcher (1H/30M/15M/5M) is now Playbook A, so LTF-ENGULF names nothing and listing a retired id in the allowlist of the one mode that can send real orders is exactly the kind of stale grant that gets overlooked. It also removes a real oddity: LTF-ENGULF was flagged unsanctioned in playbook-spec.js - present in no rulebook and no Pine script - while sitting on CONTROL's permitted list.",
  "_eval_comment": "CONFIRMED 2026-08-28 from Tradeify's own help centre (help.tradeify.co/en/articles/12853921-select-evaluation-accounts). Anoop trades 50K SELECT Evaluation only; his account TDFYSL50413184562 carries the SL/Select prefix, matching the selectEval payout tier already configured below. Every figure here is quoted, not inferred - the previous 150K numbers (9000/4500) had been in force on a 50K account, and my own earlier back-fit of start=50378.60 is REPLACED by the real 50000: back-fitting the start from the broker balance minus the ledger silently absorbs whatever the ledger is missing, and the ledger only begins 2026-08-17. A visible gap is better than a hidden one - the drift warning now surfaces it honestly. drawdownType: END OF DAY trailing, not intraday - 'intraday swings do not move the limit', but 'the limit is still enforced in real time - touching it fails the account immediately'. floorLocksAt 50100 = start+100, where the trailing floor stops rising. dailyLossLimit: null is REAL and is the dangerous part - SELECT Evaluation has NO broker-side daily loss limit, so nothing outside this app stops a bad day until the 2000 drawdown is gone. maxContractsBroker 40 is the BROKER's micro ceiling (4 mini / 40 micro); rules.json sizeCap of 2 is Anoop's own and is 20x tighter - the broker will never enforce it for him. minTradingDays 3 follows from the 40% consistency rule, not a separate gate.",
